% Working bibliography. Optionally divide internally into commented
% sections by discipline, source genre, or research phase. The rendered
% bibliography in the final document uses a single alphabetized list
% regardless of internal sectioning.
%
% Within each working section, entries are sorted alphabetically by the
% surname of the first author or by the corporate authority. Same-first-
% author works are ordered by year ascending.
%
% Citation key convention: firstcreatorYYYYshorttitle. Lowercase ASCII,
% no spaces, no punctuation, no accents. firstcreator is the surname of
% the first listed author or editor; for corporate authors it is a short
% institutional token; for legal and official instruments it is the
% jurisdiction or issuing authority. shorttitle is a short, stable,
% meaningful title token, usually one to three words. Examples:
%
%   shakespeare1603hamlet
%   cervantes1605quijote
%   aristotle1999ethics
%   plato2000republic
%   homer1990iliad
%
% Letter suffixes (a, b, c) are used only when two entries would
% otherwise have the same key even after including a short title.
%
% All non-ASCII characters are stored as direct UTF-8 codepoints
% (á, é, í, ó, ú, ñ, ç, etc.), not as BibTeX or LaTeX accent macros.
